<decision #track.topological_decision_questions.frontier_batches apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" blocks = [] durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74B>
  How should planning ask a decision forest with multiple roots?
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74B>
  <answer ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74C>
  Ask every independently answerable root or unlocked child in one bounded topological batch, then recompute after the response.
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74C>
  <evidence ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74D>
  The requested protocol must avoid serialising unrelated decision directions while retaining dependency order.
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74D>
  <confidence ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74E>
  0.99
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74E>
  <reversibility ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74F>
  moderate
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N74F>
)>

<decision #track.conditional_decision_activation.graph_nodes apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" blocks = [] durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N752>
  How should a combination of decisions create a new planning question?
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N752>
  <answer ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N753>
  Materialize a same-level conditional decision with explicit prerequisites, activation predicate, and provenance.
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N753>
  <evidence ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N754>
  A static nested tree cannot represent a question that depends on choices from multiple independent roots.
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N754>
  <confidence ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N755>
  0.99
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N755>
  <reversibility ?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N756>
  moderate
  </?01M0004E2HCGV6D5H4MA93N756>
)>
